Overview
Yango Fleet Management System is an enterprise-grade platform designed to streamline vehicle fleet operations, driver management, customer registration, and performance tracking for transportation companies. The system integrates with the Yango taxi platform API to synchronize vehicles, drivers, and car-driver bindings.

Key Business Processes
Customer Registration: Sales team members register customers by creating car and driver records simultaneously

Vehicle Management: Track all vehicles with status, fuel type, ownership, and Yango sync status

Driver Management: Manage driver profiles including license information, experience, and work rules

Car-Driver Binding: Associate vehicles with drivers for operational management

Performance Analytics: Track team and individual performance with comprehensive analytics

Team Management: Hierarchical management with Team Leaders and Team Members

Yango Integration: Seamless synchronization with the Yango platform

Features
Admin Dashboard
Complete employee management (CRUD operations)

Role-based access control (Admin, Team Leader, Team Member)

Team structure management

System-wide performance analytics

Advanced reporting and data visualization

Sales Team Features
Customer registration (car + driver)

Multi-step registration form with preview

Work rule selection for drivers

Real-time brand and model lookup via NHTSA API

Registration history and tracking

Operations Features
Vehicle management with status tracking

Driver management with license validation

Car-driver binding management

Yango platform synchronization

Search, filter, and detailed views for all entities

Performance Analytics
Team performance ranking

Individual member performance tracking

Multiple view options (pivot, chart, calendar)

Export reports as PDF

Date range filtering (today, week, month, quarter, year)

Efficiency scoring and trend analysis

Reporting
Team leader performance dashboards

Member registration counts

Yango sync status monitoring

Downloadable performance reports

Technology Stack
Backend
Node.js

Express.js

PostgreSQL

JWT Authentication

Axios for API calls

bcrypt for password hashing

dotenv for environment variables

Frontend
React

Vite

React Router

date-fns for date manipulation

html2canvas and jspdf for PDF generation

recharts for data visualization

Third-Party APIs
Yango Fleet API

NHTSA vPIC API (vehicle data)

System Architecture
The system follows a client-server architecture with clear separation of concerns:

text
Frontend (React) -> Backend API (Express) -> PostgreSQL Database
                                     |
                                     -> Yango API
                                     -> NHTSA API
API Design
All API endpoints are prefixed with /api/ and follow RESTful conventions.

Authentication: JWT-based authentication with Bearer token
Authorization: Role-based access control (RBAC)

Database Schema
Core Tables
employees
Stores all user accounts with role-based permissions.

Column	Type	Description
id	UUID	Primary key
first_name	VARCHAR(100)	Employee first name
last_name	VARCHAR(100)	Employee last name
phone	VARCHAR(30)	Unique phone number
email	VARCHAR(255)	Unique email address
password_hash	TEXT	Hashed password
role	VARCHAR(30)	admin, team_leader, team_member
team_leader_id	UUID	References employees.id
is_active	BOOLEAN	Account status
cars
Stores all vehicle information.

Column	Type	Description
id	UUID	Primary key
yango_vehicle_id	VARCHAR(100)	Yango platform vehicle ID
brand	VARCHAR(100)	Vehicle make
model	VARCHAR(100)	Vehicle model
color	VARCHAR(50)	Vehicle color
year	INTEGER	Manufacturing year
transmission	VARCHAR(30)	mechanical, automatic, robotic, variator
vin	VARCHAR(100)	Vehicle Identification Number
license_plate_number	VARCHAR(50)	Unique license plate
status	VARCHAR(30)	working, not_working, repairing, etc.
fuel_type	VARCHAR(30)	petrol, methane, propane, electricity
yango_synced	BOOLEAN	Yango sync status
drivers
Stores all driver information.

Column	Type	Description
id	UUID	Primary key
yango_driver_id	VARCHAR(100)	Yango platform driver ID
first_name	VARCHAR(100)	Driver first name
last_name	VARCHAR(100)	Driver last name
phone	VARCHAR(30)	Phone number
email	VARCHAR(255)	Email address
license_number	VARCHAR(100)	Driver license number
license_country	VARCHAR(10)	Country code
work_rule_id	VARCHAR(100)	Yango work rule ID
yango_synced	BOOLEAN	Yango sync status
registrations
Links cars, drivers, and sales employees.

Column	Type	Description
id	UUID	Primary key
car_id	UUID	References cars.id
driver_id	UUID	References drivers.id
sales_employee_id	UUID	References employees.id
registration_date	TIMESTAMPTZ	Registration timestamp
status	VARCHAR(30)	pending, completed, failed, cancelled
yango_synced	BOOLEAN	Yango sync status
car_driver_bindings
Manages car-driver associations.

Column	Type	Description
id	UUID	Primary key
car_id	UUID	References cars.id
driver_id	UUID	References drivers.id
bound_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	Binding timestamp
unbound_at	TIMESTAMPTZ	Unbinding timestamp
is_active	BOOLEAN	Active binding status
yango_synced	BOOLEAN	Yango sync status
Installation
Prerequisites
Node.js (v14 or higher)

PostgreSQL (v12 or higher)

npm or yarn

Steps
Clone the repository

bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/yango-fleet-management.git
cd yango-fleet-management
Install backend dependencies

bash
cd backend
npm install
Install frontend dependencies

bash
cd ../frontend
npm install
Create PostgreSQL database

sql
CREATE DATABASE yango_fleet;
Run database migrations

bash
cd ../backend
npm run migrate
Configuration
Backend Configuration
Create a .env file in the backend directory:

env
# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/yango_fleet

# JWT Configuration
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key
JWT_EXPIRY=24h

# Yango API Configuration
YANGO_API_URL=https://fleet-api.yango.tech
YANGO_API_KEY=your_api_key
YANGO_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
YANGO_PARK_ID=your_park_id

# Yango Work Rules
YANGO_WORK_RULE_ID=your_work_rule_id

# Server
PORT=5000
Frontend Configuration
Create a .env file in the frontend directory:

env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
Running the Application
Development Mode
Start the backend server

bash
cd backend
npm run dev
Start the frontend development server

bash
cd frontend
npm run dev
Access the application at http://localhost:5173

Production Mode
Build the frontend

bash
cd frontend
npm run build
Start the backend server

bash
cd backend
npm start
API Documentation
Authentication Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/login	Login with email/phone and password
POST	/api/auth/logout	Logout (client-side token removal)
GET	/api/auth/me	Get current user profile
POST	/api/auth/change-password	Change password
Employee Management
Method	Endpoint	Description	Access
POST	/api/employees	Create employee	Admin
GET	/api/employees	Get all employees	Admin, Team Leader
GET	/api/employees/:id	Get employee by ID	Admin, Own profile
PUT	/api/employees/:id	Update employee	Admin, Own profile
DELETE	/api/employees/:id	Delete employee	Admin
PATCH	/api/employees/:id/password	Reset password	Admin
Car Management
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/cars	Create car
GET	/api/cars	Get all cars
GET	/api/cars/:id	Get car by ID
PUT	/api/cars/:id	Update car
DELETE	/api/cars/:id	Delete car
POST	/api/cars/:id/sync-yango	Sync car to Yango
Driver Management
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/drivers	Create driver
GET	/api/drivers	Get all drivers
GET	/api/drivers/:id	Get driver by ID
PUT	/api/drivers/:id	Update driver
DELETE	/api/drivers/:id	Delete driver
POST	/api/drivers/:id/sync-yango	Sync driver to Yango
Registration Management
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/registrations	Create full registration
GET	/api/registrations	Get registrations
GET	/api/registrations/admin/all	Get all registrations (admin)
GET	/api/registrations/:id	Get registration by ID
PATCH	/api/registrations/:id/status	Update registration status
DELETE	/api/registrations/:id	Delete registration
Binding Management
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/bindings	Create car-driver binding
GET	/api/bindings	Get all bindings
GET	/api/bindings/:id	Get binding by ID
GET	/api/bindings/car/:car_id/active	Get active binding by car
GET	/api/bindings/driver/:driver_id/active	Get active binding by driver
PUT	/api/bindings/:id/unbind	Unbind car and driver
POST	/api/bindings/:id/sync-yango	Sync binding to Yango
Performance Analytics
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/performance/registrations	Get all registrations
GET	/api/performance/registrations/date-range	Get registrations by date
GET	/api/performance/summary	Get performance summary
GET	/api/performance/teams	Get team performance
GET	/api/performance/teams/date-range	Get team performance by date
GET	/api/performance/top-team	Get top performing team
GET	/api/performance/top-member	Get top performing member
Options
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/options/all	Get all form options
User Roles
Admin
Full system access

Employee management (CRUD)

Role assignment

Team structure management

View all data and analytics

System configuration

Team Leader
Manage team members

View team performance

Add/remove team members from team

Create registrations

View team registrations and analytics

Team Member
Create customer registrations

View own registrations

Track personal performance